    "text": "Let G be a group and assume that we have [x, y]3 = 1 for all x, y ∈ G. Is G′\nof finite exponent? Is G soluble? By a result of N. D. Gupta and N. S. Mendelssohn,\n1967, we know that G′ is a 3-group.                                       R. Brandl",
